{"subjectId":"cpp","id":"numeric-algorithms","title":"Numeric Algorithms","group":"STL Algorithms & Ranges","order":61,"html":"<p class=\"lead\"><code>&lt;numeric&gt;</code> covers folds and scans: sums, products, prefix sums, dot products, sequences, <code>gcd</code>/<code>lcm</code>.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-sum\"></i>Folds</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;functional&gt;\n#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;numeric&gt;\n#include &lt;string&gt;\n#include &lt;vector&gt;\n\nint main() {\n    std::vector&lt;int&gt; v{1, 2, 3, 4, 5};\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; std::accumulate(v.begin(), v.end(), 0) &lt;&lt; '\\n';                        // sum\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; std::accumulate(v.begin(), v.end(), 1LL, std::multiplies&lt;&gt;()) &lt;&lt; '\\n'; // product\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; std::reduce(v.begin(), v.end()) &lt;&lt; '\\n';                              // like accumulate, may reorder\n\n    std::vector&lt;std::string&gt; words{\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"};\n    std::string joined = std::accumulate(std::next(words.begin()), words.end(), words[0],\n                                         [](std::string acc, const std::string&amp; w) { return acc + \"-\" + w; });\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; joined &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n\n    std::vector&lt;int&gt; a{1, 2, 3}, b{4, 5, 6};\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; std::inner_product(a.begin(), a.end(), b.begin(), 0) &lt;&lt; '\\n';          // dot product\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>15\n120\n15\na-b-c\n32</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Watch out</div><p>The <em>type of the initial value</em> decides the accumulator type. <code>std::accumulate(v.begin(), v.end(), 0)</code> on <code>double</code>s truncates every partial sum to <code>int</code>; on big <code>int</code>s it overflows. Pass <code>0.0</code> or <code>0LL</code>.</p></div>\n<figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;numeric&gt;\n#include &lt;vector&gt;\nint main() {\n    std::vector&lt;double&gt; prices{1.5, 2.5, 3.5};\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; std::accumulate(prices.begin(), prices.end(), 0) &lt;&lt; ' '       // int accumulator!\n              &lt;&lt; std::accumulate(prices.begin(), prices.end(), 0.0) &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>6 7.5</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-stairs-up\"></i>Scans &amp; sequences</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;numeric&gt;\n#include &lt;vector&gt;\n\nint main() {\n    std::vector&lt;int&gt; v{3, 1, 4, 1, 5};\n    std::vector&lt;int&gt; prefix(v.size());\n    std::partial_sum(v.begin(), v.end(), prefix.begin());               // running total\n    for (int x : prefix) std::cout &lt;&lt; x &lt;&lt; ' ';\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; \"| sum[1..3] = \" &lt;&lt; prefix[3] - prefix[0] &lt;&lt; '\\n';     // range sum in O(1)\n\n    std::vector&lt;int&gt; diff(v.size());\n    std::adjacent_difference(v.begin(), v.end(), diff.begin());\n    for (int x : diff) std::cout &lt;&lt; x &lt;&lt; ' ';\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n\n    std::vector&lt;int&gt; ids(5);\n    std::iota(ids.begin(), ids.end(), 10);                              // 10 11 12 13 14\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; ids.back() &lt;&lt; ' ' &lt;&lt; std::gcd(84, 36) &lt;&lt; ' ' &lt;&lt; std::lcm(4, 6) &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n\n    std::vector&lt;int&gt; ex(v.size());\n    std::exclusive_scan(v.begin(), v.end(), ex.begin(), 0);             // sums *before* each element\n    for (int x : ex) std::cout &lt;&lt; x &lt;&lt; ' ';\n    std::cout &lt;&lt; '\\n';\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>3 4 8 9 14 | sum[1..3] = 6\n3 -2 3 -3 4\n14 12 12\n0 3 4 8 9</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Algorithm</th><th>Computes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>accumulate(f, l, init, op)</code></td><td>Left fold, in order</td></tr><tr><td><code>reduce(f, l, init, op)</code></td><td>Fold in any order (parallelisable; <code>op</code> must be associative &amp; commutative)</td></tr><tr><td><code>inner_product</code> / <code>transform_reduce</code></td><td>Σ aᵢ·bᵢ (or custom ops)</td></tr><tr><td><code>partial_sum</code> / <code>inclusive_scan</code></td><td>Prefix sums including the current element</td></tr><tr><td><code>exclusive_scan</code></td><td>Prefix sums excluding it</td></tr><tr><td><code>adjacent_difference</code></td><td><code>out[i] = in[i] - in[i-1]</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>iota(f, l, start)</code></td><td>Fill with <code>start, start+1, …</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>gcd</code>, <code>lcm</code></td><td>C++17</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>How do prefix sums answer range-sum queries in O(1)?</summary><div><p>Precompute <code>pre[i] = a[0] + … + a[i-1]</code> (size n+1, <code>pre[0] = 0</code>) once in O(n). Then the sum of <code>a[l..r]</code> is <code>pre[r+1] - pre[l]</code> — one subtraction per query.</p></div></details></section>"}